    "multi_video_column_YE3nYc": {
      "type": "multi-video-column",
      "blocks": {
        "column_4AdyC8": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/HL7ghzfQvnI",
            "title": "A Kitchen Fit For a Castle",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>Welcome to the glorious castle-home of Frieda and Javvy. This episode features a wonderfully eccentric Classic English kitchen and our very first Heirloom Dairy Table. Expect to see plenty of psychedelic floral wallpapers, quirky fabrics and homewares.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_H9YB6U": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/eUYLRaVeurM",
            "title": "Form and Function",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>Bridget and Christopher create the perfect Shaker kitchen for their Victorian family home in Wimbledon. We also learn about the origins and early days of deVOL, with a visit to our first workshop in Loughborough.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_7gmfew": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/GSHKzReJ8mg",
            "title": "Big Dreams for a Small Kitchen",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>Designing for small spaces is often challenging, but Joe gets it just right with this bold Shaker kitchen in his self-renovated cottage in County Durham. This is one for people who love a good antiques market.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_99PWC7": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/OM8A5kGx3HA",
            "title": "Paul's Kitchen",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>Our Director, Paul, renovates his dream holiday cottage in St. Ives, opting for freestanding Classic cupboards and one-room living. We also see Robin, our Managing Director, in his home workshop, crafting our new Heirloom Gaselier Light.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_ERAAB6": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/356r3GaA59w",
            "title": "A Kitchen Built on Details",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>Cool couple, Becca and Damien, update their small family kitchen in Cornwall to suit their eco-lifestyle, and our Sebastian Cox cupboards are the perfect fit. We also follow our metalsmiths at Cotes Mill as they set out to design an elegant new light switch.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_Kyf3EX": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/HzLGnkS5QPU",
            "title": "A Kitchen for Entertaining",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>A beautiful old schoolhouse home in Brixton has its rather dysfunctional kitchen updated with simple Shaker cupboards. We also meet Doug and Danielle at the end of their six-year-long journey to renovate an incredible Tudor house in Cambridgeshire.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_aTWD8b": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/lDpjinafCME",
            "title": "A Kitchen Designer's Kitchen",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>Our Creative Director, Helen, designs an eclectic mix of Classic and vintage kitchen cupboards for her Victorian home in Leicestershire. Dainty lace curtains and handcrafted ceramic decorations.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_BEc7UX": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://youtu.be/0mR-l513Nao",
            "title": "A Chef's Kitchen",
            "subtext": "",
            "text": "<p>In the final episode, we follow Rebecca and Matt's extension project as they create a Shaker kitchen fit for a family and a cook's classroom. Meanwhile, Paul and Helen convert a retro VW pickup into our deVOLkswagon food truck.</p>",
            "show_above_image": false,
            "link": ""
          }
        }
      },
